    "sample": "\u001b[?1049h\u001b[22;0;0t\u001b[?1h\u001b=\r\u001b[4mGIT-LOG\u001b[24m(1)                        Git Manual                        \u001b[4mGIT-LOG\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       git-log - Show commit logs\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mSYNOPSIS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       \u001b[4mgit\u001b[24m \u001b[4mlog\u001b[24m [<options>] [<revision-range>] [[--] <path>...]\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\n       Shows the commit logs.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       List commits that are reachable by following the \u001b[1mparent \u001b[22mlinks from the\u001b[m\r\n       given commit(s), but exclude commits that are reachable from the one(s)\u001b[m\r\n       given with a \u001b[4m^\u001b[24m in front of them. The output is given in reverse\u001b[m\r\n       chronological order by default.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n       You can think of this as a set operation. Commits reachable from any of\u001b[m\r\n       the commits given on the command line form a set, and then commits\u001b[m\r\n       reachable from any of the ones given with \u001b[4m^\u001b[24m in front are subtracted\u001b[m\r\n       from that set. The remaining commits are what comes out in the\u001b[m\r\n       command\u2019s output. Various other options and paths parameters can be\u001b[m\r\n       used to further limit the result.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page git-log(1) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"
